{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310683,"nonce":"m2BhwHf4TlUP16awrdnYs7t5r08=","title":"The RD parser's remaining gaps. Parse valid Haxe even when the compiler cannot yet honour it - the corpus is there to score that, and a ...","message":"**The RD parser is the default and the legacy fallback must go.** As of\n2026-08-25 the STDLIB parses with ZERO fallbacks. Check with: run anything and\ngrep for `RD parser failed`; the count must be 0.\n\nShipped: structure fields with access modifiers and property accessors\n(f71b4d65), `abstract class` (ecfc2c07), `abstract function` + `overload`.\n\n\nTwo of these parse to declarations the compiler cannot yet execute:\n\n- **`abstract function foo():T;`** lowers as a body-less function with a\n  declared return type -\u003e trap stub -\u003e **SIGILL/exit 139** when called, and\n  dispatch does not reach the subclass override even though one exists. It\n  needs to lower as a VIRTUAL SLOT the way an interface method does.\n- **`overload`** has no resolution: with `over(String)` and `over(Int)` in\n  scope, `over(\"a\")` calls the **Int** one and prints `int:49016888672`.\n\nI reverted both for turning \"a loud parse error\" into a crash or a wrong\nanswer, and the owner corrected it: **that is what the conformance corpus is\nFOR.** A parse error does not protect anyone -- it hides the gap from the only\nmeasurement that would ever get it fixed, and the harness already reports a\ncrash as CRASH and a wrong answer as WRONG_ANSWER. See\n[[feedback-parse-valid-haxe-let-the-corpus-score-the-gap]].\n\n\n| construct | n |\n|---|---|\n| `.` in some type/expr position | 6 |\n| `-\u003e` in a type (`?f:Map\u003cK,V\u003e-\u003eV`, `(close:() -\u003e Void)-\u003eR`) | 6 |\n| `static var` INSIDE a function body (Haxe 4.3 static locals) | 5 |\n| `=\u003e`, `*`, `\u003e\u003e`, `\u003c`, numeric literals | ~8 |\n\n\n`parse_access_and_modifiers` (rd/mod.rs) is SHARED between class fields and\nmodule-level declarations. Consuming `abstract` there broke `abstract Void` in\nStdTypes.hx -- \"expected type declaration, found 'Void'\" -- and took the whole\nstdlib back to the legacy parser. Field-only keywords belong in\n`parse_class_field`.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_rd_parser_remaining_gaps` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}